<main class="page"><article class="doc-body"><p>                                   HINTS ON CHEMISTRY FOR BEGINNERS</p><p>                                                          E. J. NWANKWO</p><p><figure class="doc-image"><div class="frame"><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></div></figure></p><p>                                                                         </p><p><strong>                     INTRODUCTION TO CHEMISTRY</strong></p><p>Chemistry is a pure science which studies the composition, the properties and the composition of matter.</p><p>The keywords from the definition above include:</p><ul><li><strong>pure science</strong></li><li><strong>properties</strong></li><li><strong>composition of matter</strong></li></ul><p>Science is an organized body of knowledge. </p><p>In other words, science deals with facts.</p><p>Facts are provable. Facts have evidences.</p><p>According to science water freezes at 0<sup>0</sup>C and boils at 100<sup>0</sup>C.</p><p>And it is so everywhere in the world.</p><p>It has been proven all over the world. </p><p>Therefore, it is a scientist fact that water freezes at 0<sup>0</sup>C </p><p>and boils at 100<sup>0</sup>C</p><p>Every scientific fact begins with observation and hypothesis.</p><p>Observations are what we see, hear, feel, smell or taste.</p><p>Hypothesis is what we think based on our observations.</p><p>Hypothesis needs experiment to prove if it is right or wrong.</p><p>If  an hypothesis is supported by several experiments, it becomes a theory and might eventually become a law.</p><p><strong>There are three pure science</strong></p><p>-1- Biology which is a study of life</p><p>-2- Physics which studies matter in relation to energy. </p><p>      Physicist are more interested in energy</p><p>-3-Chemistry.</p><p><strong>Matter is anything that has mass or weight and occupies space</strong></p><p>There is a relationship between mass and weight</p><p>Weight = Mass x acceleration due to gravity</p><p>Mathematically, W = mg</p><p>The acceleration due gravity is inversely proportional to the radius of the earth.  .</p><p>This means as radius increases, the acceleration due to gravity reduces.</p><p>The is why acceleration due to gravity is highest at the North and South poles while it is lowest at the Equator</p><p><strong>                                  STATES OF MATTER</strong></p><p>                         There are 3 states or forms of matter: </p><p>                                  	  solid , </p><p>liquid </p><p>and gas</p><p><strong>                                  COMPOSITION OF MATTER</strong></p><p>There are 3 building blocks of matter. </p><p>             They are known as the composition of matter</p><ol><li>Atom </li><li>molecule </li><li>And ion</li><li>An atom is the smallest particle of an element which can take part in a chemical reaction.</li></ol><p><strong>Key note</strong></p><ul><li>An atom is not the smallest particle of an element. </li></ul><p>This is because we have particles smaller than an atom such as proton, electron and neutron. They are called sub-atomic particles.</p><ul><li>However in chemical reactions, proton, neutron and electron are too small. </li></ul><p>So for chemical reactions, an atom is the smallest.</p><p><strong>An atom can also be defined as the smallest particle of an element which can exist and still retain all the properties that element.</strong></p><ol><li><strong>A molecule= atom + atom</strong></li></ol><p>A molecule is the smallest part of a substance which can exist alone </p><p>and still retain all the properties of that substance be it an element or a compound.</p><p><strong>There are two types of molecule</strong></p><ol><li>Molecule of an element</li><li>Molecule of a compound</li></ol><p>In molecule of an element no new substance is formed:     </p><p>    H +  H      H<sub>2</sub></p><p>However in molecule of a compound a new substance is always formed:   </p><p> Na + Cl        NaCl</p></article></main>

